      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "To be clear, this is just an issue with the Editor UI. It is not easy to workaround and prevents using parameters in certain ways, yet ought to be trivially fixable by VRChat, especially as we approach the avatar dynamics update where local ParameterDriver will be even more important.\nIf StateMachineBehaviour wasn't so darn cursed, I'd suggest to use the Debug inspector, but that is difficult to the point of not being a feasible workaround.\nYou can stack multiple drivers, like set -1, add -1 to get -2 but that gets ridiculous really quickly.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-01-08T12:36:35.939Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The ui of the parameter driver currently clamps all float values between -1 and 1 because that's what synced parameters are limited too.\nLocal paramters are however not limited to that range and you can already drive them to any value by setting it via the debug view. \nBut if you open the state aftwards the UI of the Parameter Driver clamps the value again.\ntl;dr: pleare remove clamping of local float parameters in the parameter driver ui",
